.TH SY 1
.SH NAME
sy \- Modern file synchronization tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsy\fR [OPTIONS] [<SOURCE>] [<DESTINATION>]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Modern file synchronization tool
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-size\fR \fI<MIN_SIZE>\fR
Minimum file size to sync (e.g., "1MB", "500KB")
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-size\fR \fI<MAX_SIZE>\fR
Maximum file size to sync (e.g., "100MB", "1GB")
.TP
\fB\-\-bwlimit\fR \fI<BWLIMIT>\fR
Bandwidth limit in bytes per second (e.g., "1MB", "500KB")
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-dry\-run\fR
Show changes without applying them (dry\-run)
.TP
\fB\-\-diff\fR
Show detailed changes in dry\-run mode (file sizes, byte changes) Requires \-\-dry\-run to be effective
.TP
\fB\-d, \-\-delete\fR
Delete files in destination not present in source
.TP
\fB\-\-force\-delete\fR
Force deletion even if it exceeds safety threshold (use with \-\-delete)
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Verbosity level (can be repeated: \-v, \-vv, \-vvv)
.TP
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR
Quiet mode (only show errors)
.TP
\fB\-\-perf\fR
Show detailed performance summary at the end
.TP
\fB\-\-stats\fR
Show file transfer statistics after sync completes
.TP
\fB\-\-human\-readable\fR
Show file sizes in human\-readable format (e.g., 1K, 234M, 2G)
.TP
\fB\-b, \-\-backup\fR \fI<BACKUP>\fR
Make backups of existing destination files Optional MODE: none, simple (default with \-b)
.TP
\fB\-\-backup\-dir\fR \fI<BACKUP_DIR>\fR
Directory to store backup files (default: same as destination)
.TP
\fB\-\-suffix\fR \fI<SUFFIX>\fR
Backup file suffix (default: ~)
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR~
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\-source\-files\fR
Remove source files after successful transfer (like mv)
.TP
\fB\-\-existing\fR
Don't create new files on destination, only update existing
.TP
\fB\-\-dirs\fR
Transfer directories without recursing (like rsync \-d)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<TIMEOUT>\fR
I/O timeout in seconds (for SSH connections)
.TP
\fB\-\-contimeout\fR \fI<CONTIMEOUT>\fR
Connection timeout in seconds (for SSH connections)
.TP
\fB\-i, \-\-itemize\-changes\fR
Show what changed for each file (like rsync \-i)
.TP
\fB\-j, \-\-parallel\fR \fI<PARALLEL>\fR
Number of parallel file transfers (default: 10)
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR10
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fI<EXCLUDE>\fR
Exclude files matching pattern (can be repeated) Examples: "*.log", "node_modules", "target/"
.TP
\fB\-\-include\fR \fI<INCLUDE>\fR
Include files matching pattern (can be repeated, processed in order with \-\-exclude) Examples: "*.rs", "important.log"
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\fR \fI<FILTER>\fR
Filter rules in rsync syntax: "+ pattern" (include) or "\- pattern" (exclude) Can be repeated. Rules processed in order, first match wins. Examples: "+ *.rs", "\- *.log", "\- target/*"
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\-from\fR \fI<EXCLUDE_FROM>\fR
Read exclude patterns from file (one pattern per line)
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-from\fR \fI<INCLUDE_FROM>\fR
Read include patterns from file (one pattern per line)
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\-template\fR \fI<EXCLUDE_TEMPLATE>\fR
Apply exclude template from ~/.config/sy/templates/ (can be repeated) Examples: "rust", "node", "python"
.TP
\fB\-\-verify\fR \fI<VERIFY>\fR
Verify file integrity against staged BLAKE3 verification

Modes: \- after: Verify staged content before committing each file \- only: Audit file integrity without modifying anything \- no: Disable verification (default)
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRno
.RE
.TP
\fB\-z, \-\-compress\fR \fI<COMPRESS>\fR
Compression mode for transfers \- auto: Content\-based detection with sampling (default when enabled) \- extension: Extension\-only detection (legacy) \- always: Always compress (override detection) \- never: Never compress (override detection)

\-z (no value) enables auto compression \-\-compress=MODE for explicit control
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRnever
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-links\fR \fI<LINKS>\fR
Symlink handling mode (preserve, follow, skip)
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRpreserve
.RE
.TP
\fB\-L, \-\-copy\-links\fR
Follow symlinks and copy targets (shortcut for \-\-links follow)
.TP
\fB\-X, \-\-preserve\-xattrs\fR
Preserve extended attributes (xattrs)
.TP
\fB\-H, \-\-preserve\-hardlinks\fR
Preserve hard links (treat multiple links to the same file as one copy)
.TP
\fB\-A, \-\-preserve\-acls\fR
Preserve access control lists (ACLs)
.TP
\fB\-F, \-\-preserve\-flags\fR
Preserve BSD file flags (macOS only: hidden, immutable, nodump, etc.; refused on other platforms)
.TP
\fB\-p, \-\-preserve\-permissions\fR
Preserve permissions
.TP
\fB\-t, \-\-preserve\-times\fR
Preserve modification times
.TP
\fB\-a, \-\-archive\fR
Archive mode: preserve permissions, times, and symlinks (\-rlpt) and copy everything

Deliberate divergence from rsync \-a (\-rlptgoD): owner, group, and device preservation were unimplemented stubs and are removed rather than silently ignored. All files are copied by default (no .gitignore filtering, .git directories included).

Does NOT include: \-X (xattrs), \-A (ACLs), \-H (hardlinks) \- add those flags separately.
.TP
\fB\-\-gitignore\fR
Filter files based on .gitignore rules (opt\-in)

By default, sy copies all files like rsync/cp. Use this flag to respect .gitignore rules for developer\-friendly syncs.
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\-vcs\fR
Exclude .git directories from the sync (opt\-in)

By default, sy copies .git directories like rsync/cp. Use this flag to skip version control directories for faster syncs.
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-times\fR
Ignore modification times, always compare checksums (rsync \-\-ignore\-times)
.TP
\fB\-\-size\-only\fR
Only compare file size, skip mtime checks (rsync \-\-size\-only)
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-checksum\fR
Always compare checksums instead of size+mtime (slow but thorough, rsync \-\-checksum)
.TP
\fB\-u, \-\-update\fR
Skip files where destination is newer than source (rsync \-\-update)
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-existing\fR
Skip files that already exist in destination (rsync \-\-ignore\-existing)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output JSON (newline\-delimited JSON for scripting)
.TP
\fB\-w, \-\-watch\fR
Watch mode \- continuously monitor source for changes
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-hooks\fR
Disable hook execution (skip pre\-sync and post\-sync hooks)
.TP
\fB\-\-abort\-on\-hook\-failure\fR
Abort sync if any hook fails (default: warn and continue)
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
Use named profile from config file
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-profiles\fR
List all available profiles
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-profile\fR \fI<SHOW_PROFILE>\fR
Show details of a specific profile
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-delete\fR \fI<MAX_DELETE>\fR
Maximum deletions allowed \- Absolute count: \-\-max\-delete=1000 \- Percentage: \-\-max\-delete=50% \- 0 = unlimited (default: 50%)
.RS
\fIDefault: \fR50%
.RE
.TP
\fB\-r\fR
Recursive (no\-op: sy is always recursive, for rsync compatibility)
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fB<SOURCE>\fR
Source path (local: /path or remote: user@host:/path) Optional when using \-\-profile
.TP
\fB<DESTINATION>\fR
Destination path (local: /path or remote: user@host:/path) Optional when using \-\-profile
.SH EXAMPLES
\fBBasic sync\fR
.PP
.RS 4
sy /source /destination
.RE
.PP
\fBPreview changes without applying\fR
.PP
.RS 4
sy /source /destination \-\-dry\-run
.RE
.PP
\fBMirror mode (delete extra destination files)\fR
.PP
.RS 4
sy /source /destination \-\-delete
.RE
.PP
\fBParallel transfers (20 workers)\fR
.PP
.RS 4
sy /source /destination \-j 20
.RE
.PP
\fBSync single file\fR
.PP
.RS 4
sy /path/to/file.txt /dest/file.txt
.RE
.PP
\fBRemote sync (SSH push)\fR
.PP
.RS 4
sy /local user@host:/remote
.RE
.PP
\fBRemote sync (SSH pull)\fR
.PP
.RS 4
sy user@host:/remote /local
.RE
.PP
\fBQuiet mode (only errors)\fR
.PP
.RS 4
sy /source /destination \-\-quiet
.RE
.PP
\fBVerify staged integrity before commit\fR
.PP
.RS 4
sy /source /destination \-\-verify=after
.RE
